Done. Committed as `d6d8497`. Summary:

**Issue 05 fix** (`src/entities/monster.rs:110`): `spawn_monster` now uses `rng.pick(&defs)` over the tier's defs, falling back to `MONSTERS[0]` only when the tier list is empty. Added two tests: species variety within a tier (100 spawns at tier 1 yield >1 species) and tier correctness across all depths.

**Latent bug exposed by the fix**: the stream shift made seed-42 hiscore tests hang. Root cause in `populate_monsters` (src/core/game.rs:142): the loop passed a fresh `self.rng.clone()` to `random_floor_tile` each iteration, so a proposed tile colliding with the player position never advanced the RNG — the unbounded `while placed < n` spun forever. The pre-existing `max = n + 4` was meant as an attempt cap but was misapplied to `placed` (always true). Fixed it to cap actual attempts; the success path is unchanged (still exactly `n` iterations).

All 27 tests pass.
